From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:55:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] NDS: HaltInterrupted always inline

GCC kept an out-of-line copy of it that the slice loop (RunSlicesJIT, HaltSkip,
SliceChain) called for every halted CPU: 0.5% of the emulator thread in
HeartGold (P5 profile). Code placement only: exact.
---
--- a/src/NDS.h
+++ b/src/NDS.h
@@ -521,8 +521,9 @@
     void ClearIRQ(u32 cpu, u32 irq);
     void SetIRQ2(u32 irq);
     void ClearIRQ2(u32 irq);
-    // (inline: a halted CPU's Execute asks it every scheduler slice)
-    bool HaltInterrupted(u32 cpu) const
+    // (inline: a halted CPU's Execute asks it every scheduler slice; always (patch 0220): GCC kept an out-of-line copy
+    // that the slice loop called, 0.5% of the emulator thread in HeartGold)
+    [[gnu::always_inline]] bool HaltInterrupted(u32 cpu) const
     {
         if (cpu == 0)
         {
